=== layout: two-panels

# The Model Gives a 1:1 Ratio

@left

![Lecture diagram](assets/lect10d-chromo_aneuploid/image_030.png)

@right

- Gametes: half with [*one copy*]{color=#24578F}, half with [*two*]{color=#935D00}
- Normal gamete: *one more copy*
- Zygotes: half with two copies, half with three
- [*Model answer: 50% trisomy*]{color=#007A00}

Actual outcomes: additional effects of *fertilization and survival*

=== layout: subsection

# Prenatal Testing

=== layout: one-panel

# Screening or Diagnosis?

@body

{table-style=comparison}
| Screening | Diagnostic Testing |
| --- | --- |
| [*Chance estimate*]{color=#24578F} | [*Testing sampled cells or DNA*]{color=#935D00} |
| Blood tests, ultrasound | Chromosome testing after CVS or amniocentesis |
| False positives and false negatives possible | Answers specific to the laboratory test |

[*Positive screen*]{color=#24578F}: follow-up testing, *not a diagnosis*

@citation

https://www.cdc.gov/birth-defects/diagnosis/screening-for-birth-defects.html

=== layout: one-panel

# Prenatal Blood Screening

@body

- Blood screening estimates the chance of a condition
- A triple screen measures *AFP*, *hCG*, and *estriol*
- A quad screen also measures *inhibin-A*
- An unusual result can occur in a pregnancy without the condition
- A screening result is not a diagnosis

@citation

https://www.cdc.gov/birth-defects/diagnosis/screening-for-birth-defects.html

=== layout: one-plus-two-panels

# Nuchal Translucency Scan

@left

- Ultrasound looks for extra fluid behind the fetal neck
- Used with blood tests in first-trimester screening
- Estimates likelihood; does not establish a diagnosis
- An abnormal screen can lead to an offer of diagnostic testing

@top-right

![Lecture diagram](assets/lect10d-chromo_aneuploid/image_017.png)

@bottom-right

![Lecture diagram](assets/lect10d-chromo_aneuploid/image_018.png)

@citation

https://www.cdc.gov/birth-defects/diagnosis/screening-for-birth-defects.html

=== layout: one-panel

# Diagnostic Samples

@body

{table-style=comparison}
| Sample | Where It Comes From |
| --- | --- |
| [*Amniocentesis*]{color=#D40000} | Amniotic fluid containing fetal cells |
| [*Chorionic Villus Sampling (CVS)*]{color=#007A00} | Placental tissue |
| [*Umbilical Blood Sampling (PUBS)*]{color=#B74300} | Fetal blood from the umbilical cord |

[*Sample*]{color=#24578F}: cells or DNA; [*lab test*]{color=#935D00}: what can be detected

